{"version":"CHC-v2.9.2","items":{"gf":[{"id":"gf1","text":"Number series: 3, 7, 11, 15, ?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"17"},{"v":"b","t":"19"},{"v":"c","t":"21"},{"v":"d","t":"23"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gf2","gfGraphic":true,"gfKind":"symbolCommute","text":"Shape sum: the first row shows the value of ○+□. Complete the cell with the same logic (add the same shapes; order does not matter).","correct":0},{"id":"gf3","gfGraphic":true,"gfKind":"digit7center","text":"Target with rules: one rule applies by priority (7→center; 2 and 5 together 25 → double ring; 3→star; 9→square). Given 731, on which ring does the point land?","correct":0},{"id":"gf4","gfGraphic":true,"gfKind":"masCercaRings","text":"Target: use the rules and criterion: if several apply, the ring with the **lower** ring number wins (**closer** to center). Which value is on the ring **closest** to the center? Choices: 9, 4, 5, 7.","correct":0,"gfNumOpts":[9,4,5,7]},{"id":"gf5","gfGraphic":true,"gfKind":"masLejosRings","text":"Same rules and figure. Which value is on the ring **farthest** from the center? Choices: 9, 4, 5, 7.","correct":2,"gfNumOpts":[9,4,5,7]},{"id":"gf6","text":"If NOT green implies turn the light on, and the light is off, then:","options":[{"v":"a","t":"It must be green"},{"v":"b","t":"Cannot be deduced without more data"},{"v":"c","t":"It must not be green"},{"v":"d","t":"The light is broken"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gf7","text":"Pattern: Z, Y, X, W, ?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"U"},{"v":"b","t":"V"},{"v":"c","t":"T"},{"v":"d","t":"S"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gf8","text":"A painted cube is cut into 8 equal small cubes. What is the maximum number of painted faces on a corner cube?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"1"},{"v":"b","t":"2"},{"v":"c","t":"3"},{"v":"d","t":"4"}],"correct":"c"},{"id":"gf9","text":"Series: 17, 14, 11, ? (same rule at each step).","options":[{"v":"a","t":"8"},{"v":"b","t":"9"},{"v":"c","t":"10"},{"v":"d","t":"6"}],"correct":"a"},{"id":"gf10","text":"Series: 2, 4, 8, ? (each term follows the same rule).","options":[{"v":"a","t":"10"},{"v":"b","t":"12"},{"v":"c","t":"14"},{"v":"d","t":"16"}],"correct":"d"},{"id":"gf11","text":"Series: 5, 6, 4, 5, ? (alternates +1 and −2).","options":[{"v":"a","t":"2"},{"v":"b","t":"3"},{"v":"c","t":"4"},{"v":"d","t":"6"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gf12","text":"You start at 3 and want to end at 7 using exactly two operations, one after the other. You may choose only from: −5, +2, +3, +8, −4. Which pair gives the right net change (in any order of application, adding 4 to the start to reach 7)?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"+8 and −4"},{"v":"b","t":"+3 and +2"},{"v":"c","t":"−5 and +3"},{"v":"d","t":"+2 and +2"}],"correct":"a"}],"gc":[{"id":"gc1","text":"Choose the term closest in meaning (synonym) to the stimulus.","stimulus":"ephemeral","options":[{"v":"a","t":"eternal"},{"v":"b","t":"fleeting"},{"v":"c","t":"heavy"},{"v":"d","t":"dark"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gc2","text":"Analogy: complete the relationship (verb / use).","stimulus":"book → read · food → ?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"cook"},{"v":"b","t":"eat"},{"v":"c","t":"table"},{"v":"d","t":"hunger"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gc3","text":"Choose the meaning closest to:","stimulus":"mitigate","options":[{"v":"a","t":"increase"},{"v":"b","t":"soften or reduce"},{"v":"c","t":"destroy"},{"v":"d","t":"imitate"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gc4","text":"Choose a synonym of the word in the box.","stimulus":"prudent","options":[{"v":"a","t":"impulsive"},{"v":"b","t":"cautious"},{"v":"c","t":"noisy"},{"v":"d","t":"fast"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gc5","text":"Choose the expression that best completes the sentence (discourse coherence).","stimulus":"Most voted in favor; the decision was ___.","options":[{"v":"a","t":"unanimous"},{"v":"b","t":"controversial"},{"v":"c","t":"by majority"},{"v":"d","t":"illegal"}],"correct":"c"},{"id":"gc6","text":"«Altruistic» is closest to the definition:","stimulus":"altruistic","options":[{"v":"a","t":"seeks profit"},{"v":"b","t":"acts for others' benefit"},{"v":"c","t":"avoids contact"},{"v":"d","t":"only follows orders"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gc7","text":"Opposite analogy. Complete: cold:heat = dry:?","stimulus":"cold → heat · dry → ?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"wind"},{"v":"b","t":"humid"},{"v":"c","t":"cloud"},{"v":"d","t":"winter"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gc8","text":"Choose the appropriate paraphrase (definition) for:","stimulus":"persevere","options":[{"v":"a","t":"change one's mind often"},{"v":"b","t":"keep effort despite difficulties"},{"v":"c","t":"avoid responsibilities"},{"v":"d","t":"work without rest for a single day"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gc9","text":"Logical bridge: intermediate term in a sequence (development).","stimulus":"baby → ? → adult","options":[{"v":"a","t":"adolescent"},{"v":"b","t":"retiree"},{"v":"c","t":"newborn"},{"v":"d","t":"elder"}],"correct":"a"},{"id":"gc10","text":"Metamorphosis: indicate the intermediate stage of the stimulus (larva → ? → adult).","stimulus":"caterpillar → ? → butterfly","options":[{"v":"a","t":"chrysalis"},{"v":"b","t":"leaf"},{"v":"c","t":"egg"},{"v":"d","t":"sap"}],"correct":"a"},{"id":"gc11","text":"Semantic closeness (synonym) with:","stimulus":"excessive","options":[{"v":"a","t":"too much"},{"v":"b","t":"insufficient"},{"v":"c","t":"exact"},{"v":"d","t":"weak"}],"correct":"a"},{"id":"gc12","text":"Choose the term closest to «icy / frigid» (very cold) shown in the box.","stimulus":"icy · frigid","options":[{"v":"a","t":"lukewarm"},{"v":"b","t":"glacial or very cold"},{"v":"c","t":"warm"},{"v":"d","t":"mild"}],"correct":"b"}],"gv":[{"id":"gv1","text":"Which figure completes the sequence: circle, square, circle, square, ?","options":[],"svgChoice":true,"choices":["circle","square","triangle","hex"],"correct":0},{"id":"gv2","text":"Rotation: the figure in the box, the arrow, and the star are reference. Choose among the four options the oval that matches a 90° clockwise turn relative to the star's position (reference layout).","gvGraphic":true,"gvKind":"arrowOval","correct":1},{"id":"gv3","text":"Same figure: the solid triangle occupies the same “corner type” as the sample. Choose the option showing the same relative placement (rotated like the sample).","gvGraphic":true,"gvKind":"sameTri","correct":0},{"id":"gv4","text":"Visual analogy: use the relationship between the first and third drawing. What fits logically in the blank? (inspired by sock / shoe pairs).","gvGraphic":true,"gvKind":"analogy","correct":0},{"id":"gv5","text":"Legend: circle = liquid, square = solid, hexagon = sweet. «Something sweet inside a liquid» — choose the diagram that represents it.","gvGraphic":true,"gvKind":"nest","correct":0},{"id":"gv6","text":"Perspective: two parallel lines on paper appear as:","options":[{"v":"a","t":"Always perpendicular"},{"v":"b","t":"Parallel or converging depending on perspective"},{"v":"c","t":"Always curved"},{"v":"d","t":"A single point"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gv7","text":"Sequence: triangle, circle, triangle, circle, … (pattern repeats). Which figure comes next?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"triangle"},{"v":"b","t":"circle"},{"v":"c","t":"square"},{"v":"d","t":"pentagon"}],"correct":"a"},{"id":"gv8","text":"On a standard die (faces 1 to 6), how many faces show an odd number?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"2"},{"v":"b","t":"3"},{"v":"c","t":"1"},{"v":"d","t":"4"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gv9","text":"A square: its two diagonals are drawn inside. How many points do they cross (interior, not counting vertices)?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"1"},{"v":"b","t":"2"},{"v":"c","t":"4"},{"v":"d","t":"0"}],"correct":"a"},{"id":"gv10","text":"Analog clock: from 3:00 to 6:00, the hour hand rotates, in the usual direction, approximately:","options":[{"v":"a","t":"30°"},{"v":"b","t":"60°"},{"v":"c","t":"90°"},{"v":"d","t":"180°"}],"correct":"c"},{"id":"gv11","text":"Press Play and watch the oval and reference mark after a 90° clockwise turn around the center. Which option shows how they look at the end?","gvAnimateSvg":true,"svgChoice":true,"gv11ThumbAngles":[270,180,0,90],"correct":3},{"id":"gv13","text":"Press Play. The <strong>arrow</strong> next to the oval is <strong>asymmetric</strong> (stroke like the oval) and the figure makes a <strong>single</strong> clockwise turn around the center; the text <strong>does not say</strong> how many degrees. Pick the only thumbnail that matches the <strong>final</strong> orientation (distractors are only at ±15° or −30°—compare carefully).","gvAnimateSvg":true,"gvFineRotation":true,"gvFineTargetDeg":135,"svgChoice":true,"gv13ThumbAngles":[120,150,135,105],"correct":2}],"glr":[{"id":"glr1","glrMotif":"sound","text":"Same capture criterion (pair–response, like the example in the box).","stimulus":"dog → bark · cat → ?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"tail"},{"v":"b","t":"meow"},{"v":"c","t":"fish"},{"v":"d","t":"house"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"glr2","glrMotif":"color","text":"Colors: complete the coherent pair (stimulus with arrows in the box).","stimulus":"blue → sky · green → ?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"fire"},{"v":"b","t":"grass"},{"v":"c","t":"night"},{"v":"d","t":"ice"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"glr3","glrMotif":"cook","text":"Tool–activity. Complete the second pair (as in the reference box).","stimulus":"bread → oven · fish → ?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"net"},{"v":"b","t":"tree"},{"v":"c","t":"car"},{"v":"d","t":"paper"}],"correct":"a"},{"id":"glr4","glrMotif":"key","text":"Studied pairs: if «key / door», complete the pair in the box (object: function or complement).","stimulus":"key → ?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"window"},{"v":"b","t":"lock"},{"v":"c","t":"wall"},{"v":"d","t":"floor"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"glr5","glrMotif":"sense","text":"Sensory channel (stimulus 1 → stimulus 2). Choose the appropriate sense (box and pills).","stimulus":"music → ear · aroma → ?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"sight"},{"v":"b","t":"smell"},{"v":"c","t":"taste"},{"v":"d","t":"touch"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"glr6","glrMotif":"partwhole","text":"Part and whole. Complete in the box, same scheme as in samples (not figures).","stimulus":"finger → hand · branch → ?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"tree"},{"v":"b","t":"leaf"},{"v":"c","t":"flower"},{"v":"d","t":"bark"}],"correct":"a"},{"id":"glr7","glrMotif":"origin","text":"Product–origin association (main text; pictorial guide for support).","stimulus":"milk → cow · honey → ?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"wood"},{"v":"b","t":"bee"},{"v":"c","t":"leaf"},{"v":"d","t":"ocean"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"glr8","glrMotif":"scale","text":"Text analogy (A:B = C:?). Same type of link, not a drawing substitute.","stimulus":"ocean → deep · sky → ?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"high"},{"v":"b","t":"wide"},{"v":"c","t":"distant"},{"v":"d","t":"cloudy"}],"correct":"a"}],"gq":[{"id":"gq1","gqGraphic":true,"gqKind":"numSeries","series":[2,4,8,16],"microHint":"Visual series — next number.","options":[{"v":"a","t":"18"},{"v":"b","t":"24"},{"v":"c","t":"32"},{"v":"d","t":"28"}],"correct":"c"},{"id":"gq2","gqGraphic":true,"gqKind":"numSeries","series":[3,6,12,24],"microHint":"Next term (same rule).","options":[{"v":"a","t":"30"},{"v":"b","t":"36"},{"v":"c","t":"42"},{"v":"d","t":"48"}],"correct":"d"},{"id":"gq3","gqGraphic":true,"gqKind":"numSeries","series":[17,14,11,8],"microHint":"Same rule at each step.","options":[{"v":"a","t":"5"},{"v":"b","t":"7"},{"v":"c","t":"4"},{"v":"d","t":"6"}],"correct":"a"},{"id":"gq4","gqGraphic":true,"gqKind":"symbols","symbolDefs":[["▲","2"],["■","5"]],"equationTok":["▲","+","■","+","▲"],"microHint":"Add using the legend.","options":[{"v":"a","t":"7"},{"v":"b","t":"8"},{"v":"c","t":"9"},{"v":"d","t":"10"}],"correct":"c"},{"id":"gq5","gqGraphic":true,"gqKind":"symbols","symbolDefs":[["●","4"],["◆","3"]],"equationTok":["●","+","◆","+","◆"],"microHint":"Add using the legend.","options":[{"v":"a","t":"8"},{"v":"b","t":"10"},{"v":"c","t":"11"},{"v":"d","t":"12"}],"correct":"b"},{"id":"gq6","gqGraphic":true,"gqKind":"symbols","symbolDefs":[["△","1"],["□","4"]],"equationTok":["△","+","□","+","□"],"microHint":"Add using the legend.","options":[{"v":"a","t":"7"},{"v":"b","t":"8"},{"v":"c","t":"9"},{"v":"d","t":"10"}],"correct":"c"},{"id":"gq7","gqGraphic":true,"gqKind":"dotsCompare","leftDots":11,"rightDots":7,"microHint":"Compare the groups.","options":[{"v":"a","t":"More dots on the right"},{"v":"b","t":"Equal amount on both sides"},{"v":"c","t":"More dots on the left"},{"v":"d","t":"Cannot tell"}],"correct":"c"},{"id":"gq8","gqGraphic":true,"gqKind":"dotsCompare","leftDots":9,"rightDots":9,"microHint":"Compare the groups.","options":[{"v":"a","t":"Left is greater"},{"v":"b","t":"Right is greater"},{"v":"c","t":"Equal amount on both sides"},{"v":"d","t":"One dot is missing"}],"correct":"c"},{"id":"gq9","gqGraphic":true,"gqKind":"barCompare","barPct":[35,78],"labels":["A","B"],"microHint":"Which bar is proportionally taller?","options":[{"v":"a","t":"Bar A is taller"},{"v":"b","t":"Both are equal"},{"v":"c","t":"Bar B is taller"},{"v":"d","t":"They swap if rotated"}],"correct":"c"},{"id":"gq10","gqGraphic":true,"gqKind":"fourCell","cells":[["6","12"],["2","?"]],"microHint":"Four cells: same proportion across rows or columns.","options":[{"v":"a","t":"2"},{"v":"b","t":"3"},{"v":"c","t":"4"},{"v":"d","t":"5"}],"correct":"c"}]},"gwm":[{"id":"gwm1","seq":"6 9 9 5 4","mode":"forward"},{"id":"gwm2","seq":"7 2 6 2 6 5","mode":"forward"},{"id":"gwm3","seq":"8 3 9 9 9 2","mode":"reverse"},{"id":"gwm4","seq":"9 4 6 4 3 4","mode":"reverse"}],"gsTarget":"★","gsItems":[{"id":"gs0","sym":"★"},{"id":"gs1","sym":"☆"},{"id":"gs2","sym":"★"},{"id":"gs3","sym":"●"},{"id":"gs4","sym":"★"},{"id":"gs5","sym":"◆"},{"id":"gs6","sym":"★"},{"id":"gs7","sym":"▲"},{"id":"gs8","sym":"★"},{"id":"gs9","sym":"■"},{"id":"gs10","sym":"★"},{"id":"gs11","sym":"▼"},{"id":"gs12","sym":"★"},{"id":"gs13","sym":"◇"},{"id":"gs14","sym":"★"},{"id":"gs15","sym":"○"},{"id":"gs16","sym":"★"},{"id":"gs17","sym":"◎"},{"id":"gs18","sym":"★"},{"id":"gs19","sym":"⊕"}]}